  "body": "**Stacked on #990** (#891, `issue/891-lathe-cutting-data`). Until #990 merges, this diff also shows #990's commits; this PR's own work is the last commit. Retarget to `main` happens before #990 merges (AGENTS.md \"Overlapping issues stack\").\n\nFork synced at v0.18.0 (PROCESS_VERSION 16).\n\n## What changed\n\nA lathe setup can now state the rated maximum rpm of its chuck or collet.\n\n- **Model**: `SetupDef::workholding_max_rpm: Option<f64>` (`None` means none is stated, which is the default and what every older file loads as). It is read through the new `camcraft_app::setup_workholding` module.\n- **Command**: `SetSetupWorkholdingRpm::new(world, setup, Option<f64>)` is undoable. It refuses a value that is not finite, is under 1 rpm or is over 100 000 rpm, and it refuses a no-op. It also refuses a name that is not a setup.\n- **G96**: the per-section CSS ceiling (#891's `PARAM MaxSpindleSpeed`) becomes min(tool, workholding). Both lathe posts already take the lower of that and the machine's maximum, so `G50 S` (Fanuc) and `G96 D` (Tormach) come out as min(machine, tool, workholding). **No post script changed.**\n- **G97**: an operation that turns the work (the spindle law's `turns`) at a constant rpm above its setup's limit is **refused by name** at the program gate (`verification_report`). It is never capped. Example line: `F1: turns the work at 2500 rpm (G97), over setup 'Setup1''s workholding maximum of 2000 rpm - ...`. Every post route and `verify` read this same gate.\n- **Suggestion**: the turning \"Suggest feeds & speeds\" is held to the limit, with a note, and keeps the per-rev feed.\n- **Datum transfer**: `CreateSetup` with `datum_from` keeps the source setup's rating. Dropping it would quietly lift a safety ceiling.\n- **Project file**: a new additive `workholding_max_rpm` key on a setup, with no version step. It is written only when stated. A value no command would accept is a corrupt file and is refused naming the setup.\n- **MCP**: a new tool `set_workholding_max_rpm` `{max_rpm: number|null, setup?}` in `crates/app/src/mcp/workholding_tools.rs`. It is one undo step through the same command. `get_job` setups now report `workholding_max_rpm`.\n- **UI**: a \"Workholding max rpm\" row on a setup's Settings page (value, Apply rpm, Clear rpm). It shows on a lathe or mill-turn setup, or on any setup that already states a limit. It queues `CommandKind::SetSetupWorkholdingRpm` and the drain lands the command.\n- Decisions: `docs/decisions/1031-workholding-max-rpm.md`.\n\n## Tests (pinning)\n\n- `crates/app/tests/lathe_workholding_rpm.rs`. This is a new sibling suite, because `lathe_post_css` is at 373 lines.\n  - `a_2000_rpm_chuck_clamps_g96_under_a_higher_tool_and_machine_in_both_dialects`: `G50 S2000\\nG96 S170 M03` and `G96 D2000 S170 M3` on a 12000 rpm machine, with a tool clamp of none or 3000. A tool rated lower (1500) keeps its own clamp.\n  - `a_g97_op_over_the_chuck_is_refused_by_name_never_capped`: 2500 rpm against a 2000 rpm chuck is refused at the gate and by `post_script`, naming the op and the setup. Raising the limit clears the refusal, and undo brings it back. With no limit stated, the op posts `G97 S2500` as before.\n  - `the_limit_is_one_validated_undoable_command`: insane values, a no-op and a non-setup are refused; undo and redo work; a datum transfer keeps the rating.\n  - `the_turning_suggestion_is_held_to_the_chuck`\n  - `the_limit_is_additive_in_the_project_file_and_round_trips_byte_identical`: an older file loads with none; a corrupt value is refused by name; an unstated limit writes no key.\n- `crates/app/tests/mcp_workholding.rs`: `set_workholding_max_rpm_states_clears_and_undoes_the_chucks_rating`\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/structural.rs`: `setup_page_workholding_rpm_row_structure`, the structural twin. A mill setup has no row; a lathe setup shows it; Apply lands one undo step; Clear shows once a limit is stated.\n\n## Gate\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` on head `ef57929b`: **green**, 5 steps, 0 failed, 24.1 min wall. The base is upstream/main, so it also covers #990's diff, and its plan ran every app suite, lathe_post_css, lathe_post, lathe_post_refusals, lathe_post_tormach, lathe_spindle_law, lathe_spindle_fit, lathe_spindle_keyed, project_roundtrip, setups, mcp_setup, mcp, mcp_workholding and lathe_workholding_rpm among them. The ui lib, structural twin included, passed too.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No real control was run. The posted words are checked against the Fanuc and Tormach scripts in the engine only.\n- No new golden was added, and no existing golden or snapshot PNG changed.\n- No script verb was added for the command. The MCP tool covers headless use.\n- The `camcraft-mcp` skill's tool table (`.claude/skills/`) is not updated. It is a process file, and changing it needs a PROCESS_VERSION bump, so it is left to a process PR.\n- The rating is not checked against the machine's spindle minimum. A chuck rated under the machine's minimum is not flagged.\n\nChangelog: Turning: a setup can state its chuck or collet's maximum rpm (Setups page, MCP `set_workholding_max_rpm`); G96 clamps to min(machine, tool, workholding) and a G97 turning op over it is refused by name (#1031)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #1031\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
